# ls-foundry boundary (roamvantage)

**Never** create, edit, commit, or publish files under `~/projects/ls-foundry` (or any clone of [ls-foundry](https://github.com/jeffgo10/ls-foundry)) from a **roamvantage** agent session. Engine changes belong to an **ls-foundry agent** only.

This repo consumes published `@jeffgo10/*` packages (GitHub Packages) for the 360 engine. Prefer `/update-ls-foundry-packages` after a release. App wrapper: `src/components/viewer/panorama-viewer.tsx`.

## Engine split

| In ls-foundry | In RoamVantage |
|---|---|
| Pannellum React wrapper, markers, labels/content UI, edit click-to-place | Properties/scenes/hotspots data, R2 uploads, Supabase Auth, share links, tiers, branding |

**Reject for foundry:** Next.js routes, Supabase/R2/Stripe SDKs, RoamVantage business rules.

## Consumer pins

| Package | Current pin | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `@jeffgo10/panorama-viewer` | **0.1.2** | Wrapper + `transpilePackages` + styles import |
| Other `@jeffgo10/*` | — | Only add when RoamVantage actually imports them |

## When RoamVantage needs engine work

1. Do **not** patch ls-foundry yourself.
2. Give the user a **paste-ready brief** for the ls-foundry agent (template below).
3. After publish, run `/update-ls-foundry-packages` here and wire the app.

## Paste template — ls-foundry agent

```text
## Task — <short title>

Repo: jeffgo10/ls-foundry.

### Goal
<what RoamVantage needs and why>

### Required work
1. Packages / versions to bump (e.g. packages/panorama-viewer → @jeffgo10/panorama-viewer)
2. API / type changes (props, hotspot shape, imperative handle)
3. Publish to GitHub Packages; confirm npm view dependencies

### Out of scope
- RoamVantage routes, Supabase, R2, billing UI

### Done when
- Published versions + deps verified
- Tell consumer: run /update-ls-foundry-packages in roamvantage
```

## Do not

- Edit, commit, or `pnpm publish` from ls-foundry while working in roamvantage
- Put product/backend logic into `@jeffgo10/*`
- Assume local `~/projects/ls-foundry` path aliases replace published pins in production
